Participants’ across the active-passive continuum show diﬀerent preferences for the platform-base incentives that can inspire their participation for combating misinformation [Table 8]. Active participants in both conditions show higher levels of preference for getting badges (57%) and followers (53%). In contrast, participants in the passive group report lower levels of preference for those 2 incentives, 22% and 12% respectively. The moderately active participants, similar to the participants in the passive group, have lower percentage of responses for the 2 incentives, 34% and 29% respectively.
