It is noteworthy that the distributions themselves have appear to have a pattern. We can obverse that most avatars have a ﬂat uniform distribution for their scores. However, the Mid1 realism avatars (Victor and Ilana) and Mid2-Low realism male avatar (Macaw) appear to have a normal distribution of the rank scores. But interestingly, the real humans (Rose and Rycroft) and one of the Mid2-Low realism female avatars (Bailie) have a distinct bi-modal distribution showing the divided opinion of these speciﬁc avatars in terms of the participants uncanniness perceptions.

